1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,703
All right, I'm listening.

2
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:37,912
Here's what I noticed.

3
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,165
<i>The way he moves isn't ordinary.</i>

4
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,249
Like Chiara's.

5
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:43,585
Better dig deeper, Agent Dara.

6
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:52,051
But did you know Viktor
was transferred to another prison?

7
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:53,511
When did that happen?

8
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:55,013
They didn't report it to me.

9
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,431
I only found out just now.

10
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,683
But it looks like they transferred him
the other night.

11
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,269
To the most secluded area,

12
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:03,897
and Viktor was transferred
to maximum security.

13
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:08,610
You criminals sure do talk a lot.

14
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:10,695
Boss, just relax.

15
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,865
This guy from Prague looks tough, huh?

16
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:14,783
All right, then.

17
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,326
Let's teach him a lesson.

18
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:18,620
Boss, that's enough.

19
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:21,456
You don't have to do this anymore.

20
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,666
I'll take it all!

21
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,342
I don't think I've seen her
around here before.

22
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:34,677
Maybe she's attending the wedding.

23
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:35,720
Huh?!

24
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,890
We only invited a few people.

25
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,643
Maybe she's from Chiara's side.

26
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:43,853
And you know Chiara and I only wanted
our closest friends and family

27
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:46,648
to be invited to the wedding.

28
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:51,778
Mom?

29
00:01:57,408 --> 00:02:01,621
We were just talking about
how he misses his mom.

30
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:03,915
And now they finally meet!

31
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,960
That's so nice for Rahmboy!

32
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,385
Mama Yaya?

33
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:20,431
Mom!

34
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:30,900
I've missed you.

35
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:33,319
That's Rahmboy's mother!

36
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:34,737
Rahmboy?

37
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:40,160
I've missed you so much.

38
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,375
Look how big you've gotten!

39
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:52,589
You used to be a baby crying to Mom
because you had poop in your butt.

40
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,174
Look at you now!

41
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:59,220
You're even taller than me,
aren't you, son?

42
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,471
Mom.

43
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:04,183
Mom, you're embarrassing me
in front of Aunt Tess and Uncle Mario.

44
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:08,062
Come on, Rahmboy. It's okay!
Your mom is really funny.

45
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:09,522
By the way, I'm Tess!

46
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:10,773
Tess.

47
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:11,900
I'm Mario.

48
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,736
Mario and Tess.

49
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:15,778
Mari-Tess?

50
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:18,031
What a perfect match!

51
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:21,159
Like a love team, just like QuenDrea.

52
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:24,162
Vicky, you're really
keeping up with everything.

53
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:27,206
Of course! I have a Gen-Z kid.

54
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,876
So I'm always updated
on the latest trends.

55
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:32,837
Right! Like mother, like son.

56
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:37,133
Oh, Vicky, did you know?
Rahmboy livestreams all day.

57
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:41,304
Mama Yaya.

58
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:49,646
My dear.

59
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:50,855
My dear.

60
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,246
Mama Yaya?

61
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:10,750
What do you mean?
Are you and Chiara siblings?

62
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:13,503
No, we're not. I don't get it either.

63
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:21,928
Mama Yaya raised and took care of me
when I was a child.

64
00:04:22,011 --> 00:04:25,139
She's always there
when I trained in Sicily.

65
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:29,310
The only one who's very special to me.

66
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:34,565
- Hello.
- Hello, ma'am.

67
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:39,737
Well, Vicky, it's
a double celebration after all!

68
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:40,780
Exactly! Isn't it amazing?

69
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:43,992
Of all places, you happened to reunite
with Aunt Vicky here in Albay.

70
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,120
You can just call me Mom Vicky.

71
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:49,372
Ah yes! Mom Vicky, I'm Mikoy.

72
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:50,581
- Mikoy.
- That's right.

73
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:54,168
I'm Chiara's fiancé.

74
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:57,213
Oh, really? You're getting married, dear?

75
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:02,135
Yes! To my greatest love.

76
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:06,180
Looks like I came at just the right time.

77
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:08,933
With all due respect, Mom Vicky.

78
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:11,352
How long will your vacation
in the Philippines be?

79
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:15,064
I'm never going back abroad.

80
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:17,817
I've been a domestic helper
there for so long,

81
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,403
taking care of someone else's child.

82
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:24,157
Now it's time for me
to take care of my own child.

83
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,116
Right, son?

84
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:27,702
There you go! You really are the best mom!

85
00:05:27,785 --> 00:05:30,121
That's really great to hear!

86
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:33,458
You deserve your early retirement,
Mama Yaya.

87
00:05:33,541 --> 00:05:36,586
You've sacrificed so much all these years.

88
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:42,050
I really hope you can
make it to my wedding.

89
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:44,552
Are you sure, dear?

90
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:49,432
Is that okay with you, Mikoy?

91
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:56,064
Who am I to say no
to my sweetheart's Mama Yaya?

92
00:05:56,147 --> 00:05:59,484
Of course! You're more than welcome,
Mom Vicky.

93
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:01,986
Thank you.

94
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,197
What a wonderful day this is!

95
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:09,535
Vicky, I've got some kakanin
and calamansi juice for you, too!

96
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:13,247
- Right timing!
- Go on.

97
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:14,916
Perfect timing. There's biko!

98
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:16,167
- You all are so good at that.
- How did you find out?

99
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:18,086
- How did you know?
- That's what you're good at!

100
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,462
You're still a child back then.

101
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:20,755
Come on, Vicky, let's have a snack.

102
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:21,839
Of course, Mom.

103
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,592
Aunt Vicky, have some biko!

104
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:41,359
I was assigned
to La Morte Bianca's villa before.

105
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,945
As a domestic worker.

106
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,449
I didn't even know who they were.

107
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:55,957
Until I found out
I was working for the mafia.

108
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,794
See? In-law was right all along.

109
00:06:59,877 --> 00:07:02,171
That La Morte Bianca is shameless.

110
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:09,137
You know, heaven or hell, wherever she
is now, I hope she stays there for good!

111
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:14,016
That explains why you're
the one who raised Chiara.

112
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:16,936
I raised Donatello too.

113
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:24,235
If only I could've kept them
away back then, I would have.

114
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,116
You want more, sweetheart?

115
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,493
This is so good.

116
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:39,333
This is so good. It really is, Mom!

117
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,044
Go ahead, eat up!

118
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,045
All right.

119
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,756
Maybe you want more. You can take mine.

120
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:48,676
Really? Sure!

121
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:40,061
Just a little more.

122
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:42,522
I'ts okay to cry.

123
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:44,565
It won't make you weak.

124
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:51,739
Here, have something to eat. Go on!

125
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:54,116
You'll be training again later.

126
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,952
Eat up!

127
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:07,713
Here's yours.

128
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,298
Thank you.

129
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,937
Are you okay, Mom Vicky?

130
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,440
Of course, Mikoy!

131
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:31,028
I'm just so happy to be with my child,

132
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:33,447
and also this girl I raised as my own.

133
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:40,413
It's a small world after all.

134
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:03,311
You guys take care of our guests.

135
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:08,316
Perfect!

136
00:10:08,399 --> 00:10:09,108
Are you Viktor?

137
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:10,109
Relax, boss!

138
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,737
Senator wants us to welcome you.

139
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,537
Chill out, boss!

140
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,622
Sir Vik!

141
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:23,706
Easy, boss!

142
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:26,751
Easy, boss!

143
00:10:27,418 --> 00:10:28,336
Sir Vik!

144
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,635
Mr. Viktor!

145
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:38,262
Give us a smile!

146
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,139
Okay, one more!

147
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:43,684
Let's go. Just leave him.

148
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:46,437
Sir Vik!

149
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:53,736
Are you okay, boss?

150
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:02,495
I'm staying right here.

151
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:09,835
Could Senator Quentin
finally be getting back at Viktor?

152
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,921
Now's finally his chance!

153
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:16,008
Ever since the Moravianos
arrived in the Philippines,

154
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:20,596
the Sinigang Cartel's operations
have come to a halt!

155
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:25,142
His side hustle got shut down,
so now he's getting revenge!

156
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:30,731
And he can get back at him
by making Viktor's life miserable

157
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,942
while his case is in court.

158
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:40,324
But wouldn't going after Viktor
put Senator Quintin's ties

159
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:45,996
to the Sinigang Cartel at risk?

160
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:49,458
Unless he has other plans for Viktor.

161
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:56,424
Just like us, we're keeping him because
he has valuable information for us.

162
00:11:58,175 --> 00:12:03,848
You mean, Senator Quintin
needs something from Viktor?

163
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:06,976
What could it be?

164
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:11,439
Referrals to criminals in Europe?

165
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:13,399
Business contacts?

166
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:20,990
For a businessman posing
as a public servant?

167
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:25,119
What you are saying is not impossible.

168
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:38,549
Sen. Look at this.

169
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:47,725
YESTERDAY

170
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,060
You know what?

171
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:53,522
If this is effective for Chiara,
well and good!

172
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:55,900
And if not,

173
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:59,737
well, we still have Donabel.

174
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:06,368
Oh, that's panful!

175
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:07,786
Especially that one.

176
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:13,792
You know what?

177
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:17,213
I can't remember any stories from Chiara
about her Mama Yaya.

178
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,464
Really?

179
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:22,801
Maybe because Chiara
was still young back then.

180
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:26,138
She can't remember anything. Right?

181
00:13:27,097 --> 00:13:28,474
That's true.

182
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:29,517
Or it also can be

183
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,103
after all that Chiara
went through as a child,

184
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:35,356
she doesn't want to revisit
those memories anymore.

185
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:37,441
Can be.

186
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:38,859
If you think about it,

187
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:41,278
since she was a child,
La Morte Bianca has been training her

188
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,239
to fight and hold a gun.

189
00:13:43,822 --> 00:13:46,909
Too much, right?
Her childhood is so traumatic.

190
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,746
Let's just think about this.

191
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:55,834
Look at Chiara now. She's so happy.

192
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:57,628
That's right, Dad.

193
00:13:58,128 --> 00:14:00,548
After everything we've been through,

194
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:03,259
I've never seen her this happy before.

195
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,846
And because of that,

196
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:12,393
we need to celebrate
with a delicious dinner!

197
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:13,727
- Yes!
- Yes!

198
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,814
Okay, okay! I'll head to the market
while it's still light,

199
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:19,441
and I'll pick up something to grill.

200
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,568
- Ooh!
- Wait, wait!

201
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:23,654
Honey, could you buy me lots of tomatoes?

202
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,948
- I'm making a salad.
- Okay!

203
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:28,701
Uncle Mario, get me some hotdogs too.
For the kolokoys.

204
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:31,495
All right, sure!

205
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:35,332
Hey! Easy on the biko!

206
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:36,375
Why?

207
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:37,543
I missed this!

208
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,587
Can you not? Mind your own snack!

209
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:41,463
Wait, wait. Captain Pepe,

210
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:43,674
you've been so quiet.

211
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:46,135
He ate a lot too!

212
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,219
He probably hasn't digested it yet, huh?

213
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:48,721
It's not like that.

214
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:50,055
Then what?

215
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:55,019
It's just that Aunt Vicky
isn't from around here.

216
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:56,979
Why did she suddenly show up?

217
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,732
Of course, she just got here.

218
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:02,443
Yes, and Chiara knows her.

219
00:15:02,526 --> 00:15:03,736
She seems nice.

220
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:05,487
And trustworthy too.

221
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:11,118
I hope so. I hope you're right.

222
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,876
This is unbelievable, Mama Yaya.

223
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:22,004
I can't believe we're seeing
each other again!

224
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:25,466
What a coincidence, right?

225
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,677
This is no coincidence, dear.

226
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,639
None of this is a coincidence.

227
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:33,724
Didn't I tell you before?

228
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:37,811
There's something destined for each of us.

229
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,940
It's time, Chiara.

230
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:44,610
It's time for you to lead the Concordat.

231
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:50,991
Whatever you have here,

232
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:53,744
you need to leave it all behind.

233
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,288
As soon as possible.

234
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,238
Bro.

235
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:35,202
I just hope that
after you and Sis Chiara get married,

236
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,580
I hope nothing changes.

237
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,794
What's going to change?

238
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,006
I don't know.

239
00:16:47,631 --> 00:16:48,799
It's just…

240
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:51,010
You know how it is.

241
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:53,512
You and Sis Chiara might get busy.

242
00:16:55,597 --> 00:16:56,765
And…

243
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:59,810
Well, you might not
have time for me anymore.

244
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:02,104
We won't be able to hang out anymore.

245
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,440
We won't be able to vlog together.

246
00:17:05,774 --> 00:17:08,152
Or go fishing here by the river.

247
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:13,073
Listen, Rahmboy.

248
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,534
Even after Chiara and I get married,

249
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:18,370
I'll still be your brother, okay?

250
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:21,248
And you, you'll still be a pain in my ass!

251
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,794
Geez. You're something else, Bro.

252
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,796
But okay.

253
00:17:28,422 --> 00:17:29,381
You're right.

254
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,593
- You're right, anyway.
- Nah, I'm just kidding!

255
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:34,428
Of course, nothing will change!

256
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:37,931
You know that, my Rahmboy! Oh, you.

257
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:41,018
Now, enough being dramatic, okay?

258
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,019
- I'm not!
- Will you?

259
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:42,978
I'm not being dramatic.

260
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,229
- Yes, you are!
- This is nothing!

261
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:46,774
I'm just making sure.

262
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,570
How do you do this again?

263
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,031
Oh, Bro!

264
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,575
Let's vlog first.
This might be our last one.

265
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:59,036
There you go again with the drama.

266
00:17:59,119 --> 00:17:59,995
What was that?

267
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,413
- Huh?
- There's someone back there.

268
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:02,581
- Where?
- They're wearing black!

269
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:03,499
- Huh?!
- There they are!

270
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,042
- Bro! Bro! Wait!
- Just come with us, bro!

271
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,335
- Do not resist.
- Bro!

272
00:18:07,002 --> 00:18:07,669
Quit fighting!

273
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:08,837
What's happening?

274
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:09,922
Help me!

275
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:11,298
Chiara!

276
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:13,425
Mom! Dad!

277
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,260
Okay, okay, okay!

278
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,386
Get in!

279
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:18,639
Chiara!

280
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:25,229
All right! Sounds like a success!

281
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,606
Enjoy, Bro Mikoy!

282
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,108
Really?

283
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:30,818
Kidnapping again?

284
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,486
Prague already traumatized me!

285
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:33,570
Hey!

286
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:35,572
Let me go!

287
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:37,783
Help! Hey!

288
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,493
Where are the girls?

289
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:41,870
I told you they're not answering!

290
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:45,332
Even the singers aren't picking up.

291
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:46,875
They ghosted us. Angelito!

292
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:48,836
Call this number, will you?

293
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:50,129
Angelito?

294
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:51,922
Oh, Bro, just keep quiet for a minute.

295
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:53,382
Hey!

296
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,175
I said quiet!

297
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:58,720
Even the dancers and the girls
I contacted have canceled.

298
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,597
Because we haven't paid
the down payment yet!

299
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:03,142
We're only just starting
to pool our money.

300
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:05,269
Just put it on my tab for now, okay?

301
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,812
See? That's what I'm talking about.

302
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,856
Borrowing money again!

303
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:12,734
Hold still! It's not even yet. Wait!

304
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,404
Do I really need this?

305
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,868
You know, Sis Chiara, you're so beautiful!

306
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:22,536
Bro Mikoy is so lucky to have you.

307
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:28,250
But I'm just as lucky to have him
and all of you.

308
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,919
Especially to the best maid of honor ever!

309
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:37,718
Here!

310
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:40,846
Let's solve this problem of yours.

311
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:42,598
Solve our problem?

312
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:43,599
Yes!

313
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:45,559
You haven't even contributed!

314
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:47,686
Exactly! You haven't even chipped in!

315
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:50,063
This is my contribution!
I'm making the calls!

316
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,900
- Okay, then.
- Cocoy!

317
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:55,360
You've been drinking this whole time,
and you haven't contributed anything too!

318
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,528
Right!

319
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,700
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Okay, okay, we're good!

320
00:20:01,783 --> 00:20:03,327
We will behave, we promise!

321
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,494
It's okay now.

322
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:06,914
Don't mess with Cocoy!
Those muscles will be the death of you.

323
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:07,748
We're screwed.

324
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,087
Wait, I think that's them!

325
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:16,048
- l'll get it.
- No, I'll get it! I'll get it!

326
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:19,760
Give me that chair.
Chiara, come sit here for a bit!

327
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:21,553
What's happening?

328
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,098
Let's hide.

329
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,234
What is that?

330
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:37,027
Here it is!

331
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:01,760
Wow!

332
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:11,061
Wow!

333
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:13,433
Hello, in-law!

334
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:15,185
In-law.

335
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:20,148
Is Chiara there?

336
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:23,068
Aw, too bad she's not here.

337
00:23:23,151 --> 00:23:26,154
Come on! It's her bridal shower.

338
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:30,951
<i>Wait a minute.</i>
<i>Do you need anything from her?</i>

339
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:33,578
Or is something wrong?

340
00:23:33,662 --> 00:23:34,955
Is something bothering you?

341
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:38,792
Nothing! I just wanted to check in on her.

342
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:41,503
Oh, she's definitely happy!

343
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:43,964
She's so excited for her wedding.

344
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:48,135
That's good to hear! Right?

345
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:51,429
I'm happy that our children is happy!

346
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:52,556
Oh.

347
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:55,600
Ah, okay, in-law! Thank you so much!

348
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:56,852
Take care over there. Good night!

349
00:23:56,935 --> 00:23:59,354
Oh, hey! You take care, too.
Wait, I have something--

350
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,524
Hello?

351
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:05,443
In-law?

352
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:13,451
<i>They've stolen so many years</i>
<i>from you, my child.</i>

353
00:24:14,911 --> 00:24:17,581
<i>I won't do away</i>
<i>with your happiness for now.</i>

354
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:22,294
<i>You deserve to be happy, Chiara.</i>
<i>My daughter.</i>

355
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:25,172
<i>Viktor,</i>

356
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:27,549
<i>wherever you are,</i>

357
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:31,011
<i>promise me you'll come back.</i>

358
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:55,577
<i>There's something destined for each of us.</i>

359
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:58,997
<i>It's time for you to lead the Concordat.</i>

360
00:25:09,758 --> 00:25:12,260
Why did you really come back, Mama Yaya?

361
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:14,471
You know why I came back.

362
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:22,354
Let's see who you're hiding, Sean.

363
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:31,112
The world really is a small place, huh?

364
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:33,365
Who would've thought your Mama Yaya
would turn out to be Rahmboy's mother?

365
00:25:33,448 --> 00:25:35,659
Even I was surprised.

366
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:39,913
How come you never told me
about your Mama Yaya?

367
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:44,209
To be honest, I just never thought
we'd see each other again.

368
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:46,378
I'm glad you found each other again.

369
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:47,504
Right?

370
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:51,132
Let me go,

371
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:53,468
so we can talk normally, Carlota. Please.
